WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.210
I told my robot: put jam on the bread.

2
00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.550
It picked up the whole jar

3
00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:06.850
and put it on the bread!

4
00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:10.190
The robot did exactly what I said.

5
00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.720
Today: how to give a robot

6
00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:15.380
exact instructions.

7
00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:19.050
A robot is not like a friend.

8
00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:21.330
A friend can guess what you mean.

9
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.640
A robot can’t guess.

10
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:25.780
It does exactly what you

11
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:27.280
say, step by step.

12
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.740
A list of exact steps in order

13
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:31.880
is called an algorithm.

14
00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:34.490
Brushing your teeth has an algorithm.

15
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:36.820
Wet the brush, add

16
00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.420
toothpaste, brush, then rinse.

17
00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:42.160
The order matters too.

18
00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:44.650
If you rinse first and add

19
00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:46.710
toothpaste last, it goes wrong.

20
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.240
Robots need the right steps,

21
00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:50.800
in the right order.

22
00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:53.800
Here is a robot on a grid.

23
00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:56.600
It has three cards: forward,

24
00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:59.020
turn left and turn right.

25
00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.200
Turning does not move it.

26
00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:03.470
It only changes the way it looks.

27
00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:05.270
Quick check!

28
00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:07.290
The robot looks up.

29
00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:09.100
The target is on its

30
00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:10.600
right, one square away.

31
00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:12.680
Which card comes first?

32
00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:15.100
Turn right first.

33
00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:18.100
Now the robot faces the target.

34
00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:21.670
Then one forward card, and it gets there.

35
00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:25.910
In the app, open Program a robot.

36
00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.010
Put the cards in order and press Run.

37
00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:31.750
Try grids one, two and three.

38
00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:33.490
Your turn.

39
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.780
I say only: tidy the desk.

40
00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:40.880
Who understands that, a friend or a robot?

41
00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:42.800
A friend.

42
00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:45.880
Remember: an algorithm is

43
00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.780
exact steps, in order.

44
00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:50.970
A robot does exactly what you say.

45
00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:53.310
And the order of the steps matters.

46
00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:56.970
Try it yourself: program a person.

47
00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.960
Write exact steps to draw a simple house.

48
00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.700
Give them to a friend or someone at

49
00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.280
home, and see what they draw!
